cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its result data, please cite the paper under preferred-citation, and the Zenodo record for the archived data."
title: "JAX-ESHN: a JAX/TensorNEAT implementation of ES-HyperNEAT for diagnosing the quadtree substrate-discovery bottleneck"
abstract: >-
  JAX-ESHN is a JAX-based ES-HyperNEAT implementation built to characterize, rather than
  to resolve, the quadtree substrate-discovery bottleneck that prevents population-level
  vmap vectorization. The repository ships the implementation, a PUREPLES CPU baseline
  harness, an HSHG ablation, the committed per-seed result data, and analysis and
  verification scripts that recompute the paper's tables.
